<title>INDONESIA: Jababeka issues $150 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Jababeka issues $150 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian industrial estate firm PT Kawasan Industri Jababeka said on Monday it had issued $150 million worth of floating rates notes through Netherland-based subsidiary Jababeka International BV.</p>
<p>The loan has a maturity period of three years with interest at two percent above six month LIBOR, the firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>The firm said the issue was fully subscribed.</p>
<p>It said parts of the proceeds would be used to increase its land base in the Cilegon industrial estate in West Java and to acquire a 67.5 percent stake in property property firms PT Batavia City Realty and PT Batavia Perkasa.</p>
<p>The statement did not give further details.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
